mode: "100644"
text: "# The Retention Ladder — climb four rungs, in order\n\nOn Shorts you don't earn reach by being clicked — there's no thumbnail, no CTR. You earn it by\n**not being skipped.** Every Short is written backwards from the swipe. Four rungs, each a\nverified 2026 gate; miss a lower rung and the higher ones never get measured.\n\n## Rung 1 — Stop (the first 1–3 seconds)\nBeat the swipe. The first frame's only job is to make the next second inevitable.\n- **On-screen text + a striking visual on frame one** — before any slow intro. (Most watch on\n  mute, so the opening must read silently.)\n- State the stake/payoff immediately; no logo, no \"hey guys,\" no build-up.\n- Target: **~75%+ Viewed vs Swiped Away.** If you're under 50% at 10–15s, the hook is the problem.\n- (Opener craft → hook-writer.)\n\n## Rung 2 — Hold (≈70%+ average percentage viewed)\nRetention is the king metric. Keep them to the end — ideally to a replay.\n- **Relentless pacing:** advance the idea every 1–2 seconds; cut dead air; one idea per Short.\n- **Caption everything** (2 lines/frame, ~32–42 chars/line, away from edges) — lifts completion\n  and feeds Shorts search.\n- **Loop with intention:** the last frame should connect conceptually to the first so the average\n  view duration crosses 100% (replays = a top signal). A callback line makes the first second\n  mean more on rewatch.\n\n## Rung 3 — Angle (information gain)\nDistribution at scale now requires novelty. The Anti-Repetitive AI suppresses recycled formats.\n- Bring a **genuinely unique angle** — a fresh take, first-party data, a specific experience.\n- Don't clone your own last hit or whatever's trending verbatim. **Volume without novelty is a\n  negative.** Fewer, sharper Shorts beat a flood of templated ones.\n\n## Rung 4 — Bridge (turn discovery into channel growth)\nShorts are a **discovery engine.** Because Shorts and long-form are decoupled, the bridge is\n**manual, not algorithmic** — design it deliberately.\n- Make the channel surface worth subscribing to when one Short pops.\n- Point viewers to long-form/offers via the channel, pinned comment, or a follow-up Short — and\n  via **keyword-rich titles/descriptions** so the Short ranks in Shorts search.\n- For business channels, the real benchmark is whether Shorts show up as a **traffic source on\n  your long-form** — check it natively. (Long-form engine: youtube-long-form.)\n\n## The beat sheet a Short script should fill\n```\n0:00–0:03  STOP    on-screen text | striking first visual | spoken hook\n0:03–end   HOLD    one idea, fast cuts, captions, intentional loop\n (whole)   ANGLE   the unique take that makes it worth wide distribution\n close     BRIDGE  conceptual loop + a reason to visit the channel/long-form\nship with: keyword-rich title + description (Shorts search), captions, Altered-Content\n           disclosure if AI-generated\n```\n"
